{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdfCGwQciXpHsJu61giX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014qm64nUtq2GphiqwQ3fhKs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> docs/harness/log.md <<'EOF'\n\n## 2026-11-02: position filters configurable per device\n\nFifteen filter settings (invalid, zero, duplicate, outdated, future, past, accuracy, approximate, static, distance, max speed, min period, daily limit, daily limit interval, skip limit) are now device keys in `config/Keys.java`. The `FilterHandler` resolves each one for the position's device with `AttributeUtil.lookup`: device attribute, then groups, then server config, then the key default. The handler constructor is now `FilterHandler(cacheManager, statisticsManager)`.\n\nWhat I learned: the keys had `null` defaults, so they now have explicit defaults (false, 0 or 0L) to avoid unboxing errors. Because `filter.future` defaults to 86400 seconds, a position far in the future is now filtered even with no configuration; set it to 0 to disable. `filter.globalDailyLimit` stays server-only.\n\nLeft: no test covers the daily limit, min period, distance or max speed settings per device; they use the same lookup, but only the invalid, zero, future and group cases are tested.\nEOF\ngit status --short","description":"Append implementation log entry and show status"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3357,"cache_read_input_tokens":76724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3357},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0a13a83a-6ada-485d-86d1-a04dd9b6d457","uuid":"cd30e0a3-57be-43ed-868d-d949758c8d48","timestamp":"2026-11-02T06:52:13